WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.256
Not every public detail creates the same risk.

00:00:04.256 --> 00:00:12.545
Evaluation begins with sensitivity: could the information expose identity, access, location, relationships, internal operations, or security controls?

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:21.281
Then consider who can use it, how easily it can be combined, and what harm could reasonably follow.

00:00:21.281 --> 00:00:23.297
Context changes risk.

00:00:23.297 --> 00:00:34.273
A generic technology name may be low sensitivity, while the same detail combined with an exposed service and unpatched version may require action.

00:00:34.273 --> 00:00:40.322
A public office address differs from a private residence or precise routine.

00:00:40.322 --> 00:00:46.370
Aggregation risk occurs when individually ordinary details combine into a sensitive picture.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:55.554
Usernames, photos, calendars, vendor references, and technical records can reveal relationships or timing that no one source states directly.

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:59.810
Analysis should minimize unnecessary aggregation, especially about individuals.

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:02.275
Assess timeliness and accuracy.

00:01:02.275 --> 00:01:08.771
Old records, cached pages, reused addresses, and abandoned profiles can misrepresent current conditions.

00:01:08.771 --> 00:01:16.163
Validate important findings with authoritative or independent sources and record when each source was observed.

00:01:16.163 --> 00:01:19.075
Separate relevant findings from noise.

00:01:19.075 --> 00:01:28.708
A useful finding connects to a legitimate security, privacy, safety, or business objective and has enough evidence to support action.

00:01:28.708 --> 00:01:33.860
Popularity, novelty, or personal curiosity are not measures of relevance.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:38.116
Prioritize by likelihood, potential impact, exposure, and confidence.

00:01:38.116 --> 00:01:41.476
Describe uncertainty and avoid alarmist conclusions.

00:01:41.476 --> 00:01:54.245
Remediation should be proportionate: correct a stale page, restrict a document, secure an account, assign an asset owner, or investigate an exposed service through authorized internal processes.
